  "answer_text": "No. Cato Sockets do not support jumbo frames on LAN ports. If a 9000-byte frame arrives on a LAN port, the Socket will handle it based on the DF (Don't Fragment) flag: if DF is not set, the Socket will accept the packet and fragment it to the 1500-byte MTU; if DF is set, the Socket will drop the packet and send an ICMP Fragmentation Needed message back to the sender.",
